package secretstore // import "github.com/abigotado/agent-clis/core/secretstore"

Package secretstore stores one secret per (service, account) pair in the
operating system's credential store: the login keychain on macOS, Credential
Manager on Windows, and a Secret Service provider on Linux. It never falls back
to a file.

A Store is opened with Open and addressed by a Key. Failures are *Error values
whose Kind says what the caller should do next; every Kind has a sentinel
that errors.Is matches. Error text never contains secret bytes, the Service or
Account of the key, or text produced by the operating system.

The first Open with valid options fixes the process-wide Interaction mode.
A later Open with the other mode fails with ErrInvalidArgument, including when
that first Open itself failed; an Open with invalid options fixes nothing.

On Linux the session bus address is DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS when it is set,
and then only a unix: address is used; any other transport is refused and does
not fall back. When it is unset or empty the address is $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bus,
as libdbus does, but only if XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is an absolute path and bus there
is a socket itself, not a symlink, owned by the effective user. Otherwise Open
fails with ErrUnavailable, and the error never names the path. No bus is ever
launched.

Callers that save a credential while another process may read or rewrite it
should hold their own lock around Save and around reads that must be consistent
with it; the package does not provide cross-process locking.

On macOS the Security framework receives the secret in an immutable CFData
that is released without being zeroed; only the Go copies are zeroed, on a
best-effort basis. On Linux the D-Bus library copies the secret into message
buffers it does not zero, and the Secret Service session encryption only hides
the secret from a passive observer of the session bus; only the Go copies are
zeroed, on a best-effort basis.

Package secretstoretest provides an in-memory fake and a behaviour suite that a
Store implementation must pass.

CONSTANTS

const MaxSecretBytesLimit = 128 << 10
    MaxSecretBytesLimit is the largest MaxSecretBytes an Options value accepts.


VARIABLES

var (
	ErrNotFound            = errors.New("secretstore: not found")
	ErrAccessDenied        = errors.New("secretstore: access denied")
	ErrInteractionRequired = errors.New("secretstore: interaction required")
	ErrUnavailable         = errors.New("secretstore: unavailable")
	ErrReadOnly            = errors.New("secretstore: read-only")
	ErrContended           = errors.New("secretstore: contended")
	ErrTooLarge            = errors.New("secretstore: too large")
	ErrCorrupt             = errors.New("secretstore: corrupt")
	ErrCanceled            = errors.New("secretstore: canceled")
	ErrInvalidArgument     = errors.New("secretstore: invalid argument")
)
    The sentinels errors.Is matches for each Kind except KindOther.


FUNCTIONS

func DisableCoreDumps() error
    DisableCoreDumps sets the soft and hard core-file size limits to zero so
    a crash cannot write secrets to disk. It does nothing on systems without
    RLIMIT_CORE. The limits can only be raised again by a privileged process.


TYPES

type ACLRepairer interface {
	// RepairAccess needs InteractionAllowed and trusts only the running binary.
	RepairAccess(ctx context.Context, key Key) error
}
    ACLRepairer is implemented by the macOS store and the in-memory fake.
    It rewrites an item so the running binary can read it again.

type Error struct {
	// Op is the operation: open, exists, load, save, delete, or repair.
	Op string
	// Backend is keychain, credman, secretservice, memory, or none.
	Backend string
	// Kind is the classification errors.Is matches through Unwrap.
	Kind Kind
	// Status is the operating-system status code, or 0 when there is none.
	Status int64
	// Reason is the provider condition, or empty when there is none.
	Reason Reason
}
    Error is the error every Store method returns for a store failure. Its text
    is built only from the fixed fields below, so it cannot carry a secret,
    a key, or provider text.

func (e *Error) Error() string
    Error returns "secretstore: <op> (<backend>): <kind>[ status <n>][
    <reason>]". An Op, Backend or Reason outside its closed set renders as
    "other".

func (e Error) GoString() string
    GoString renders %#v of an Error or *Error, with a value receiver so both
    print the same sanitized fields as Error, without a leading "&", and never
    echo an unknown Reason, Op or Backend.

func (e *Error) Unwrap() error
    Unwrap returns the sentinel for the error's Kind, or nil for KindOther.

type Interaction int
    Interaction says whether the store may ask the user for anything.

const (
	// InteractionNever is the default: the store fails with
	// ErrInteractionRequired instead of prompting. Agents always run here.
	InteractionNever Interaction = iota
	// InteractionAllowed lets the store show unlock and approval prompts. Use
	// it only in explicit interactive flows.
	InteractionAllowed
)
type Key struct {
	// Service identifies the caller, such as "youtrack-agent-cli": 1-64 bytes
	// of ASCII letters, digits, '.', '_' and '-', starting with a letter or
	// digit.
	Service string
	// Account distinguishes secrets of one service, such as a profile name:
	// 1-128 bytes of valid UTF-8 with no control character, no U+241F, and no
	// '#'. Accounts are case-sensitive and wildcard characters are ordinary.
	Account string
}
    Key names one secret.

type Kind int
    Kind classifies a failure by the action the caller should take next.

const (
	// KindOther is a failure no other kind describes.
	KindOther Kind = iota
	// KindNotFound means no item exists for the key.
	KindNotFound
	// KindAccessDenied means the item exists but this code identity may not
	// read it.
	KindAccessDenied
	// KindInteractionRequired means the store needs user interaction, such as
	// unlocking, and the Interaction mode is InteractionNever.
	KindInteractionRequired
	// KindUnavailable means no backend is reachable on this system, or the
	// store cannot be used from this process, such as inside a sandbox that
	// denies keychain access (see ReasonKeychainUnusable). It never means the
	// credential is absent: a caller must not suggest re-authenticating and
	// must not treat it as KindNotFound.
	KindUnavailable
	// KindReadOnly means the store refused a write that reads are allowed.
	KindReadOnly
	// KindContended means the item was replaced while Save was running.
	KindContended
	// KindTooLarge means a secret exceeds the configured or backend bound.
	KindTooLarge
	// KindCorrupt means stored data could not be decoded.
	KindCorrupt
	// KindCanceled means the user dismissed an interactive prompt.
	KindCanceled
	// KindInvalidArgument means a key or option was rejected before any store
	// access, or an Open conflicted with the process-wide mode.
	KindInvalidArgument
)
    The kinds an *Error can carry. KindOther is the zero value and has no
    sentinel; its Status or Reason describes the failure.

func (k Kind) String() string
    String returns a stable lower-case name for the kind.

type Options struct {
	// MaxSecretBytes bounds Save and Load; it must be 1..MaxSecretBytesLimit.
	MaxSecretBytes int
	// Interaction is the process-wide interaction mode.
	Interaction Interaction
}
    Options configure Open.

type Reason string
    Reason names a provider condition behind an *Error. It is a closed set:
    provider message text never becomes a Reason.

const (
	ReasonServiceUnknown Reason = "service-unknown"
	ReasonNameHasNoOwner Reason = "name-has-no-owner"
	ReasonNoReply        Reason = "no-reply"
	ReasonNotSupported   Reason = "not-supported"
	ReasonIsLocked       Reason = "is-locked"
	ReasonNoSession      Reason = "no-session"
	ReasonNoSuchObject   Reason = "no-such-object"
	ReasonAccessDenied   Reason = "access-denied"
	// ReasonTooManyMatches means items for one key were still there after the
	// bounded number of removal rounds.
	ReasonTooManyMatches Reason = "too-many-matches"
	// ReasonKeychainUnusable means the keychain cannot be used from this
	// process, as inside a sandbox that denies keychain access: the check
	// before an operation was refused as a malformed call, so a search that
	// finds nothing there says nothing about the credential. It accompanies
	// KindUnavailable and never means the credential is absent: a caller must
	// not suggest re-authenticating and must not treat it as not found.
	ReasonKeychainUnusable Reason = "keychain-unusable"
	ReasonOther            Reason = "other"
)
    The closed set of reasons. The empty Reason means none was recorded.

type Store interface {
	// Exists reports whether an item exists. It returns no secret.
	Exists(ctx context.Context, key Key) (bool, error)
	// Load returns a copy of the secret; the caller zeroes it after use.
	Load(ctx context.Context, key Key) ([]byte, error)
	// Save stores secret, replacing any existing item. An empty secret is
	// ErrInvalidArgument and one above the bound is ErrTooLarge, both before
	// the store is touched.
	Save(ctx context.Context, key Key, secret []byte) error
	// Delete removes the item. Deleting a missing item succeeds.
	Delete(ctx context.Context, key Key) error
}
    Store keeps secrets in the platform credential store. Every method returns
    an *Error for a store failure, a context error for a canceled context,
    and an error matching ErrInvalidArgument for an invalid key.

func Open(ctx context.Context, opts Options) (Store, error)
    Open returns the native store for this operating system. It never returns a
    file-backed store; where no backend exists it fails with ErrUnavailable.

    The first Open with valid options in a process fixes the Interaction mode,
    even if that Open then fails (for example on a canceled context); Open with
    invalid options fixes nothing. A later Open with a different mode fails with
    ErrInvalidArgument. Open performs no recovery of interrupted writes.

